A||||4||Ralfy9862||Stereo Subwoofer||||8||
Z||000000||Ralfy9862||10-04-2000||08:59 PM||||I recently installed a aftermarket pioneer stereo deck in my 87 gt fastback and cant get the original factory subwoofer to work with it. Can it even be done? HELP ME!||||reg||8
Z||000001||tgowens||10-04-2000||10:13 PM||||wire the two pink wires (both of them)from the sub amp to the yellow wire on the cars wiring harness (not the radio adapter harness) -- that way it will work when in the accessory or on position with the key. -- that's all there is to it.........you probably tried to wire the pink wires to the blue power antenna wires from the radio - that is not enough power to operate the sub.......<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                        <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-05-2000||05:31 PM||||Not to make you mad or anything, But, I think it is eaisier to cut the auto on lead comming from the harness that plugs into your factory harnes, and hook it to the ingition on lead on the same harness. I just think thats a little easier because you can pull it out of the car and work on it on a table or somthing as opposed to having to work in the small headunit area.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_Freak||10-05-2000||10:39 PM||||I used a 30 amp relay from Radio Shack.  Hook up the switched power, the remote wire from the stereo, and then the two pink together...  This way it's not alway on, only when the head unit is on.||||reg||3
Z||000004||wkayl||10-06-2000||10:34 AM||||This site tells yopu how to wire it with a relay<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.radio.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.radio.html</A> ||||reg||1
